/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 90 0 R
/T (The objective of this project is to develop a Number Guessing Game using the C programming language. In this game, the computer randomly generates a number within a specified range, and the user is required to guess that number. The program provides hints such as whether the guessed number is even or odd, too high or too low. The game continues until the user correctly guesses the number. The program also counts the number of attempts taken by the user to guess the correct number. This project helps in understanding basic C programming concepts such as random number generation, loops, conditional statements, and user input/output operations.)
/E (The objective of this project is to develop a Number Guessing Game using the C programming language. In this game, the computer randomly generates a number within a specified range, and the user is required to guess that number. The program provides hints such as whether the guessed number is even or odd, too high or too low. The game continues until the user correctly guesses the number. The program also counts the number of attempts taken by the user to guess the correct number. This project helps in understanding basic C programming concepts such as random number generation, loops, conditional statements, and user input/output operations.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
